<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows $59.1 mln at Aug 29.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows $59.1 mln at Aug 29.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $59.1 million surplus on August 29 in the commercial forex market according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON AUGUST 29</p>
<p>Exports: $167.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $190.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $465.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $382.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $59.1 million</p>
<p>AUGUST DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.386 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.537 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.698 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $4.075 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.472 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
